§ `Sections 670 and 671 -- Formal defects in jury process`

-- src:13298 | 670 Judgment shall not be stayed or reversed after verdict on an indictment
-- src:13299 | (a) by reason of any irregularity in the summoning or empanelling of the jury; or
-- src:13300 | (b) for the reason that a person who served on the jury was not returned as a juror by a sheriff or other officer.
@ref s 670 (src:13298-13300)
DECLARE `s 670 the ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 670(a) an irregularity in the summoning or empanelling of the jury`
    `s 670(b) that a person who served on the jury was not returned as a juror by a sheriff or other officer`
    `s 670 some other ground`

-- src:13298 | 670 Judgment shall not be stayed or reversed after verdict on an indictment
-- src:13299 | (a) by reason of any irregularity in the summoning or empanelling of the jury; or
-- src:13300 | (b) for the reason that a person who served on the jury was not returned as a juror by a sheriff or other officer.
@ref s 670 (src:13298-13300)
GIVEN `a verdict has been returned on an indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 670 the ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 670 the section bars staying or reversing the judgment on the ground` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a verdict has been returned on an indictment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Judgment shall not be stayed or reversed after verdict on an indictment"
        IF ground EQUALS `s 670 some other ground` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "(a) by reason of any irregularity in the summoning or empanelling of the jury; or (b) for the reason that a person who served on the jury was not returned as a juror by a sheriff or other officer"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13302 | 671 No omission to observe the directions contained in any Act with respect to the qualification, selection, balloting or distribution of jurors, the preparation of the jurors’ book, the selecting of jury lists or the drafting of panels from the jury lists is a ground for impeaching or quashing a verdict rendered in criminal proceedings.
@ref s 671 (src:13302-13302)
DECLARE `s 671 the directions` IS ONE OF
    `s 671 the qualification of jurors`
    `s 671 the selection of jurors`
    `s 671 the balloting of jurors`
    `s 671 the distribution of jurors`
    `s 671 the preparation of the jurors’ book`
    `s 671 the selecting of jury lists`
    `s 671 the drafting of panels from the jury lists`
    `s 671 some other directions`

-- src:13302 | 671 No omission to observe the directions contained in any Act with respect to the qualification, selection, balloting or distribution of jurors, the preparation of the jurors’ book, the selecting of jury lists or the drafting of panels from the jury lists is a ground for impeaching or quashing a verdict rendered in criminal proceedings.
@ref s 671 (src:13302-13302)
GIVEN `there is an omission to observe directions contained in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      directions IS A `s 671 the directions`
      `the verdict was rendered in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 671 the section bars treating the omission as a ground for impeaching or quashing the verdict` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`there is an omission to observe directions contained in an Act` AND `the verdict was rendered in criminal proceedings`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No omission to observe the directions contained in any Act ... is a ground for impeaching or quashing a verdict rendered in criminal proceedings"
        IF directions EQUALS `s 671 some other directions` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "with respect to the qualification, selection, balloting or distribution of jurors, the preparation of the jurors’ book, the selecting of jury lists or the drafting of panels from the jury lists"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 672 -- Saving powers of court`

-- The saving counts from the moment immediately before April 1, 1955: the day on which a power, authority, practice or form must be shown to have existed is 31 March 1955.
-- src:13304 | 672 Nothing in this Act alters, abridges or affects any power or authority that a court or judge had immediately before April 1, 1955, or any practice or form that existed immediately before April 1, 1955, with respect to trials by jury, jury process, juries or jurors, except where the power or authority, practice or form is expressly altered by or is inconsistent with this Act.
@ref s 672 (src:13304-13304)
GIVEN `the day on which the power or authority of a court or judge, or the practice or form, is shown to have existed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672 the power, authority, practice or form existed immediately before April 1, 1955` MEANS
    IF Day `the day on which the power or authority of a court or judge, or the practice or form, is shown to have existed` EQUALS Day (Date 31 3 1955)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names only the moment "immediately before April 1, 1955"; a showing on another day does not say what existed then

-- src:13304 | 672 Nothing in this Act alters, abridges or affects any power or authority that a court or judge had immediately before April 1, 1955, or any practice or form that existed immediately before April 1, 1955, with respect to trials by jury, jury process, juries or jurors, except where the power or authority, practice or form is expressly altered by or is inconsistent with this Act.
@ref s 672 (src:13304-13304)
GIVEN `the power or authority is one that a court or judge had, or the practice or form is one that existed, immediately before April 1, 1955` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is with respect to trials by jury, jury process, juries or jurors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power or authority, practice or form is expressly altered by or is inconsistent with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672 the Act leaves the power, authority, practice or form unaltered` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the power or authority is one that a court or judge had, or the practice or form is one that existed, immediately before April 1, 1955` AND `it is with respect to trials by jury, jury process, juries or jurors`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any power or authority that a court or judge had immediately before April 1, 1955, or any practice or form that existed immediately before April 1, 1955, with respect to trials by jury, jury process, juries or jurors"
        IF `the power or authority, practice or form is expressly altered by or is inconsistent with this Act` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where the power or authority, practice or form is expressly altered by or is inconsistent with this Act" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
